# Leaks the sanitiser reports that are not ours to fix.
#
# Narrow on purpose. Turning leak detection off entirely would be one
# line and would also switch off the only thing here worth having, so
# each entry names what it covers and why it stays.

# Qt keeps per-application state alive until the process exits and does
# not free it: the QML type registry, the logging category registry, and
# the platform plugin's own singletons. These are one-time allocations,
# not growth, and are reported at exit rather than during the run.
leak:libQt6Core
leak:libQt6Qml
leak:libQt6Quick
leak:libQt6Gui

# The plugin loader holds the platform plugin open for the life of the
# process; unloading it at exit would run destructors against a torn-down
# graphics stack.
leak:QFactoryLoader

# glibc's name service switch caches the modules it dlopen'd. Reachable
# for the life of the process by design.
leak:__nss_module_load
